The following crates under crates/ are vendored from Obscura and remain under
their original Apache-2.0 license (see crates/<name>/Cargo.toml and the
top-level LICENSE file):

  obscura, obscura-browser, obscura-cdp, obscura-dom, obscura-js,
  obscura-mcp, obscura-net, obscura-render

Local modifications to the vendored tree (the "DSH delta"):
  - crates/obscura-mcp/src/lib.rs: added `browser_web_search` MCP tool and the
    public `serp_search`/`SerpResult` helpers (keyless SERP search).
  - crates/dsh-obscura-server/: new crate providing the `mcp` and `serp`
    command-line entry points.

Third-party vendored dependencies under vendor/ (taffy, cosmic-text) keep their
own licenses as distributed by Obscura.

Modifications Copyright 2026 FFS SASU

This tree is vendored into the nexus repository (https://github.com/this-rs/nexus)
under obscura/. Further modifications there:
  - crates/dsh-obscura-server/ renamed crates/obscura-server/ (binary
    `obscura-server`, same `mcp` and `serp` subcommands); its harness-specific
    integration pieces (installer, web-seam bridge, profile patches) removed.
  - crates/obscura-mcp/src/lib.rs: MCP serverInfo name set to `obscura`.
  - Cargo.toml of every crate: workspace-inherited keys and dependencies
    written out explicitly, as the crates are members of the nexus workspace.
  - crates/obscura-js: a thread-local isolate observer (set_isolate_observer,
    clear_isolate_observer) so an embedder can terminate a cancelled page's
    JavaScript from another thread; deno_core and v8 pinned to exact versions.
  - crates/obscura-mcp: dispatch, RpcResponse and BrowserState's page-task
    pump made public, BrowserState::clear_termination added, and
    serp_search_at (serp_search against a results page given by URL), so
    nexus-tools can run the browser in process with its own transport.
  - crates/obscura-render: tests/layout_test.rs, whose fixtures are not
    vendored, gated behind a feature nothing enables.
